<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The slipcase media type, for shared-mime-info.

  SPEC 4 names `application/x.slipcase+zip` and the extension `.slpc`, and
  reserves no magic bytes: a container is identified by opening it and finding a
  conformant metadata member, which is not a question this database can ask. The
  glob is therefore the only identification available.

  This says the same thing `slipcase-desktop` says in its own copy, and the
  duplication is deliberate. Either product has to work with the other absent,
  and two packages cannot ship the same path — dpkg refuses the second install
  outright. Different filenames, one merged type: shared-mime-info takes the
  union of every package in the directory, so installing both is not a conflict
  and not a redefinition.

  **No icon element, and that is the cost of the arrangement rather than an
  oversight.** The icon named for a media type is one file at one path, and
  whichever package shipped it would collide with the other on the same rule.
  `slipcase-desktop` ships it. Where only this package is installed a container
  draws as a plain archive, which is true — it is a ZIP — and is a cosmetic loss
  rather than a functional one. The fix when both products ship together is a
  `slipcase-common` package owning the type and the icon, which is a change in
  two other repositories and not this phase's.
-->
<mime-info xmlns="http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/shared-mime-info">
  <mime-type type="application/x.slipcase+zip">
    <comment>Slipcase container</comment>
    <!--
    True and useful. A container is a ZIP, so an archive tool can open one and a
    desktop that knows nothing of slipcases still has something to offer. It
    does not cost the glob: where a name matches `*.slpc` and the content sniffs
    as `application/zip`, shared-mime-info takes the glob, because the
    magic-matched type is the parent rather than the child.
    -->
    <sub-class-of type="application/zip"/>
    <glob pattern="*.slpc"/>
  </mime-type>
</mime-info>
